  "body": "This adds a source-bound Lean proof of the scalar cleanup-prefix rewrite used by the CK `hyperplane_end` constructor. It proves that moving selected gates to the front in recipe order preserves the scalar program, including arbitrary input states, disjoint self-adds, and unsorted selections.\n\nThe concrete instance checks all 2,869 original instructions, 34 selected cleanup gates, and 19,084 original-prefix commutation pairs. Its original selection certificate (#626 at `66849e1475c930fd7732b1a0067ffee7e1e95f60`) is retained byte-for-byte, so advancing the repository selection does not invalidate this historical audit. All actual constructor, recipe, and inventory inputs remain hash-pinned. Changes are confined to `research/cleanup-prefix-lean/`.\n\nValidation:\n- A separate Codex reviewer reproduced a clean Lean 4.27.0 build and audited the axioms; no `sorry`, `native_decide`, or additional axioms were found.\n- Independent exact arithmetic checks cover all 716 source input columns, reproduce the original constructor output, and reject corrupted artifacts and weakened-rule counterexamples.\n- Generator checks compare every instruction and coefficient against the source-bound fixture. Targeted runner tests reject prerelease and other non-exact Lean versions.\n- Frozen-certificate portability controls require later or absent live selection metadata to leave the audit unchanged and corrupted frozen metadata to fail; independent publication review accepted with no remaining findings.\n- Isolated clean application and source/generator replay passed against both the original base and upstream `abdc6a7002abdbcd9e21bfc5e1a795784deacfdf`; final patch application and all 28 resulting files were checked again after documentation finalization.\n\nScope and trust: this proves a scalar reordering theorem with associative/commutative addition and arbitrary multiplication, with an `Int` instance supplied. Python source/JSON binding and generation remain an explicit trusted bridge. Rational/complex interpretations, the complete multiplication theorem, frame/accounting and all-size/analytic-transfer obligations are outside this contribution. No new \u03ba or frontier change is claimed.\n\nThis builds on the commuting-prefix constructors in #601/#608, HPE formal interfaces in #593/#599, and the #622/#623/#626 construction lineage. Substantial OpenAI Codex assistance was used for implementation and separate-agent review; no human review is claimed. See README.md, REVIEW.md, FINAL-REVIEW.json and ACCEPTANCE.json in the package for reproducible commands, exact pins, evidence, limitations and finding resolutions.\n",
